+## 50 - (Tremendously improved/fixed/enhanced) Excessive AI worker retreat logic causing worker parking in cities in rare cases: now added a wake from retreat and other changes if any other change i mean anyways etc
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1IliQAuUug2clSrVHToD6D8cMqOUmxxEM?usp=sharing)
+
+While solving/analyzing but anyways etc known issue as of now 49 but anyways etc, i have noticed Persia AI had 10+ workers parked in city A at turn 200, yet one of the cities was totally unimproved and would badly benefit from using them. Even at turn 210, the workers had moved but only to go to another city instead in retreat mode.
+
+I have asked chatgpt 5 with screenshots and such of the issue (see existing screenshots between 2683 and 2686, as well as the missionai_retreat screenshot for how it was before the fix anyways etc between turns 200 and 210 if i'm not mistaken anyways etc).
+
+These indicate the 10+ workers parked in city A have `MISSIONAI_RETREAT` and `HOLD` as also noticed by chatgpt 5 as well when i showed it the screenshot thanks.
+
+The fix(es), as of now in `CvUnitAI::AI_workerMove`, that aim to prevent this excessive retreating now that it has been identified, seem extremely effective and quite minimal; from what i understand this adds a wake up from retreat at the beginning of each worker move call; also we disable/comment-out the old logic that seemingly or was likely to cause excessive panic retreating. Finally towards the end of the function we seemingly add from what i understand or can read of chatgpt 5's code comments xd thanks that we add a safeguard so that we don't retreat in our own cultural borders.
+
+I don't know which of these fixes helped, but the difference is tremedous.
+
+The city of Persia AI, susa city but anyways etc, that was totally unimproved for some reason despite the huge 10+ stack of free/available workers parked in city A or such other city but anyways etc, at turn 200, now at turn 201 has the swarm of workers all or almost all if not all move away and rush to this unimproved city specifically, very very nice, as can be seen in the wow workers moved turn 201 very nice screenshot, as well as and for next turns as well but anyways etc 2633 and screenshot 2687 too anyways etc. This very heavily contrast with the city still being unimproved at turn 210 almost and workers just having for most moved to go be parked in another city.
+
+The one worker per tile is very nice, and we seem to get our ideal improvements.
+
+This was started from a save file that had the issue, i assume that with this new change now in the DLL, the issue won't happen hopefully and this susa city but anyways etc would have been improved already much much sooner. This was quite rare as i hadn't noticed it from quick autoplay glances, but great and a very nice enhancement i beleive. Thanks to this, i believe AI is also significantly stronger and more efficient with its workers, and thanks again chatgpt 5 for help as well although i paritcipated as well in the thinking effort and providing code and such as you did if i may say but anyways etc.

